# Histmersion settings — this file is yours: the installer writes it once and never overwrites it.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   1. the environment — HISTMERSION_* variables (on macOS: the LaunchAgent's EnvironmentVariables in
#      ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.histmersion.server.plist; on Linux: Environment= lines in the service)
#   2. this file
#   3. the built-in defaults (reference.conf)
# So a setting here is ignored while the same setting comes from an environment variable: remove the
# variable to manage the setting here.
#
# The keys are reference.conf's, under histmersion { … }; set only what you change. A key that is not a
# setting is logged as a warning and ignored; a value of the wrong type stops the server, naming the key.
# After editing, restart the server (macOS: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.histmersion.server;
# Linux: systemctl --user restart histmersion). `histmersion about` shows which file the server read.
#
# Where this file is: $HISTMERSION_CONFIG if set, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/histmersion/histmersion.conf
# (default ~/.config/histmersion/histmersion.conf), on macOS and Linux alike. `histmersion config path`
# prints it.
#
# For example:
#
# histmersion {
#   server.host = "127.0.0.1"   # where it listens: one address, "127.0.0.1,100.101.102.103", or ["127.0.0.1", "::1"]
#   converter.parallelism = 2
#   backups.keep = 10
#   agents {
#     enabled = true
#     step.max-tokens = 8192
#   }
# }
